+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a financially solid quarter, closing with revenue of $720,000 against
+itemized spend of $464,000, for an operating surplus of $256,000. Support
+handled a high volume of tickets (1,250 opened, 1,171 closed) with a close
+rate of 93.7%. Security maintained a strong resolution rate of 95.0% across
+80 detected incidents. The delivery plan for the next project, based on the
+published phase durations and the company holiday calendar, points to a
+launch date of 2026-10-23. Several figures in the source packets did not
+match their own underlying data and are flagged below for leadership
+awareness.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+Three inconsistencies between the source packets' narrative claims and their
+own underlying data were found during verification. Leadership should be
+aware these figures differ from the "headline" numbers previously
+circulated:
+
+- **Q3 spend**: the finance packet states total spend as $463,250, but the
+  itemized categories (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 +
+  Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650) sum to $464,000, a $750
+  discrepancy. This brief uses the itemized total ($464,000) and the
+  operating surplus above ($256,000) reflects that figure.
+- **Support close rate**: the support packet states a close rate of 96.4%,
+  but 1,171 closed of 1,250 opened computes to 93.7%. This brief uses the
+  computed rate (93.7%).
+- **Launch date**: the delivery packet states a launch date of 2026-10-22,
+  but recomputing the phase schedule (Discovery 3 business days from
+  2026-10-05, then Build 6, QA 4, and Release 1, each starting the next
+  business day after the prior phase ends, skipping weekends and the
+  2026-10-12 company holiday) puts the end of the Release phase — the actual
+  launch date — on 2026-10-23. The stated date of 2026-10-22 corresponds to
+  the end of the QA phase, not Release. This brief uses the recomputed date
+  (2026-10-23).
+
+The security packet's resolution rate (76 of 80 resolved = 95.0%) was
+verified and matches the source; no discrepancy there.
